apple just blew our minds at their  jam-packed spring-loaded event  where they blew through announcements  faster than ever before  like brand new air tags new software and  financial services  apple tv ipad and the new 24-inch imac  that vadim got  spot on in yesterday's video and more  but since they packed so much into just  one hour  they didn't have time to mention  everything including m1 mac  upgrades that i'm personally very  excited for so here's  every new product and upgrade apple  released but didn't mention  during their event let's start out with  some hardware  apple announced the upgraded apple tv 4k  with the a12 bionic processor  and 4k high frame rate support and with  that  a brand new remote which is likely even  more exciting  since people have been complaining about  the old one for years  this thing is made out of solid aluminum  and ditches the touch surface for a  click pad that doubles as a touch  surface  so you get the best of both worlds for  fast navigation  and new scrolling gestures so you can  easily find the perfect spot in a movie  as well as rearrange buttons with  universal remote support  now of course they announced that at the  event and they said it's gonna cost 179  for a 32 gigabyte model but what they  didn't mention  is that the remote is fully compatible  with the original apple tv  4k and even the 2015 apple tv hd  and they didn't say that you can  actually buy this new remote  by itself for 59  so there is no need to buy a whole new  apple tv kit  now if you do want to buy one but you  don't want the 4k model they also didn't  mention that this remote is coming  with the a8 equipped apple tv hd for 149  bucks but with that said i would  definitely spend the extra 30 bucks  for the a12 4k model now the next one  isn't  fully confirmed since the listings  haven't yet went live  but with a really new cool magic  keyboard with the touch id built  in that comes with a higher end 24 inch  imacs those will likely be sold  separately and we can guess what the  price will be as well  that is because apple mentioned in fine  print that you can get this keyboard as  an  option for the base model new imac now  the current magic keyboard comes in at  99  so this one will definitely cost more  due to the needed  extra sensors and the secure enclave  encryption chip  but there is no way that it will cost  any more than say a hundred bucks  extra because then the base price would  be way too close  to the 1499 higher tier imac once you  add the additional  keyboard option so it will likely cost  149 dollars to 199  and at that price point it could be  worth it for easy multi-user sign in  for apple pay for authentication and  siri autofill  the big question is if apple will wait a  bit to offer it standalone like with the  imac pro keyboard  or if they will allow it to be used on  m1 max or any t2 equipped max let me  know in the comment section if you'd be  willing to pay  149 bucks or even 199 dollars  for this new touch id enabled keyboard  now for those of you who don't care for  a built-in stand that isn't height  adjustable  even though apple didn't mention it  there is thankfully a vasa mount  capable 24 inch four and a half k imac  available to order  now apple has a special page for these  and they don't come  with the stand included so it doesn't  seem that you can swap the regular stand  for a vase amount like you can on the  imac pro  instead it looks like the vase amount is  built in so you'll want to make sure  that you buy  this specific one if you need it prices  are exactly the same as the regular 4.5  k  imac so you won't save anything but  thankfully it won't cost you any extra  either  and there's no risk to the mount messing  up like it did for many users online  with the imac pro and now for what i am  personally most excited about  and that is improvements to the m1 mac  mini  when apple announced the m1 mac mini  last year it was a jaw dropping machine  coming in at only 699 dollars and  packing way more performance than a  similarly equipped intel one  that costs over twice the price both in  cp performance and especially in  graphics performance people  were shocked even though it was the  cheapest m1 machine it also performed  the best  and ran the coolest as well but there is  one big problem for many mac mini lovers  that stopped them from upgrading and  that's the fact that the 10 gigabit  ethernet option was no longer  available if you chose an m1 equipped  mac mini  that meant that you had to use a pricey  adapter to get 10 gigabit ethernet  and one of your ports were gone and with  that they run hot  often with loud fans and they aren't  reliable as  built-in ones either well thankfully  during apple's event  they went ahead and added 10 gigabit  ethernet options to the m1 mac  minis even to the base spec 1 which is  amazing  this means that we can now use one to  replace our imac pro  since we need the 10 gigabit ethernet  port to connect to our fast media server  and since the 24 inch imac doesn't have  this option  this means that the mac mini is the only  current m1 mac that has it  we previously expected 10 gigabit  ethernet in an upcoming  m1x mini but we weren't certain but we  now know that the more powerful  upcoming macs including the 28 or 30  inch imac  will have this option which is great  that also means that you can have  a super powerful and completely silent  machine  that costs as low as 799  with this really fast and consistent  wired connection  the next things the apple didn't  announce were brand new accessories  along with the brand new magic keyboard  and white apple has new cases  for the iphone 12s we have amethyst  capri blue  cantaloupe and pistachio color options  for apple silicon cases  and if you're into the leather cases  there is one new color  deep violet if you're like me and you go  caseless  but with a wallet for the convenience  and extra grip apple is also offering  theirs in this new  deep violet color we also have new  accessory colors for ipads with the  smartfolio and smart covers now  available in white  mallet green and electric orange and the  mini cover  only comes in the latter two new color  options  along with that we have new colors for  apple watch bands  and a completely new band as well if  you're a fan of the braided solo loop  like i  am we have new pistachio and electric  orange colors  and for the standard loop we also have  that pistachio color  but also cantaloupe and tamales blue  options  for the basic sport band we have that  cantaloupe as well as mallard green and  capri blue  and for the nike sport bands apple added  chlorine blue and green  iron stone and black and hasta with  light  options the one brand new apple watch  band  is a little crazy for me both in looks  and in price tag  and that's because it's a hermes branded  one called  jumping single tour it comes in at a  massive 319 dollars for a band  made out of textile woven nylon and is  available in five colors which i don't  want to pronounce  but they're all very vibrant and apple  says that they seem to jump  off the wrist of the wearer it also  seems like we have some new colors for  other hermes watch bands but i can't  confirm if these came out today  since i don't follow these 500 watch  bands  next is a brand new color for apple's  beats studio 3  over-the-ear headphones which launched  way back in 2017  but feature active noise cancellation  and the w1 chip  now available in the limited edition  neon green color  in collaboration with cycleworld and  rapper don toliver  for 349 bucks and lastly  there is one more change to ipads this  year the apple  wasn't fully clear about they mentioned  that we now have 5g support which is  great  since speeds and reception are much  better but they didn't say  that they hiked up the price for the  modem enabled  models it used to cost 150 to get  an lte ipad but it now costs 200  so 50 is more than before making a base  ipad pro with 5g  now 1 000 and that sucks for people who  may not even have 5g in their city or  country  we're making an in-depth video comparing  the new 2021 ipad pros compared to the  previous 2020s so click that circle  above  if you want to check that out and to  help us reach our goal of 1 million  subscribers before the end of 2021  and check out another great video right  over there thank you guys for watching  this has been max and i'll see you in  the next video  [Music]

